    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Tom goes into town every Saturday. He goes by bus because he does not have a car. The bus stop is near his house, and the journey takes twenty minutes."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "First, Tom goes to the market. He buys apples, bread and cheese. The apples are two pounds for a bag. He likes the market because the food is fresh and the people are friendly."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Next, he goes to a clothes shop. He wants a new T-shirt for his brother, but the shop is closed. There is a sign on the door: Closed on Saturday afternoon. So Tom walks to a different shop. There he finds a green T-shirt for eight pounds."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "At one o'clock, Tom has lunch in a small café. He has a cheese sandwich and a glass of orange juice. After lunch, he goes to the library and returns two books. He goes home at four o'clock. He is tired but happy."
      }
    ]
